codemap 9
tour feature-edit-tour
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human, reading a tour in the window, who finds a note wrong, a name or group that no longer fits, or a call the tour should also show. Goals: the map is the second channel beside the source, and the human audits what the agent mapped. The run before this feature: the window added, removed and moved steps one at a time, but renaming a tour, regrouping it, changing its kind and every note were Console commands (tour-rename, tour-group, tour-note, step-note) that take the step index the tours command prints, not the 1.1 numbers in the window. Two designs were built and run on a promoted fixture and on this repo's promote tour. The build-tour wizard's pages (Name, Steps, Notes, Apply): a step's note sat on its own page, away from the step it describes, and a one-note fix walked four pages. The kept one is a single page: the tour's name, kind, group and note; the step outline with each step's note field under it, the calls a step makes opened as deep as wanted and ticked to add them by promote's rules; a Changes list, and a bar counting what Apply will do with a red line for every note a removal loses. Apply changes the map in one step or not at all and reopens the tour unsaved. Escape in a field only leaves the field; with changes pending, escape keeps them and says cancel discards them; a click anywhere on a step's row ticks or unticks it, and a click in its note field never does.

